hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to  another edition of ask Evan in today's  episode I'm going to answer questions  from one of my favorite breeders in the  char who wrote in asking about whether I  have a home office or go to an office to  work so the specific question was I've  tried working from home but haven't been  as successful as it's been at the office  now people at home want me to work from  home as if it's also spend more time  with me what do you suggest for me work  from home or have an office so a couple  points for you it's a great question a  lot of entrepreneurs go through the same  thing and stretch if you're a solo  entrepreneur or you manage a team that's  remotely we don't have to go into an  office because people there so you get  the choice as to whether to go to an  office or not I can share with you my  experience and hopefully that helps you  make your decision as to what to do I  found that I'm more productive when I  have an office that I go to and when I'm  there I do my work and I'm more  productive than if I'm trying to do it  from home I find it's easy to get  distracted when you're at home you can  go to the fridge and get some food and  you can hang out and you might get  sidetracked by a home project that you  need to get done it's just so easy to  get distracted you need to have really  strong discipline and ideally you want  to make it easier to get your work done  and not force yourself to get your work  done so I find going to an office helps  with that regard the second thing is  having boundaries and I find it's again  easy for people to overstep those  boundaries if you are at home so I don't  you have children or not if they're  knocking on your home office door and  then and they want to come in you know  you can say you're working but then  you're going to feel really guilty  afterwards right because you're not  spending time with them and then that's  going to decrease your productivity of  doing that work because you're feeling  so guilty for returning them away or you  let them come in and you know play in  your office and again that's kind of  taken away from your work time so having  those boundaries is important and it's a  lot easier to do it when you have to  have a physical office to go to the last  thing I found is it a lot of  entrepreneurs will blur the lines  between personal  office and you want to make sure that  your personal time is for you that  you're spending time with your family  and proven yourself and your business  time is focused on the business if  you're the kind of entrepreneurs always  always always you know working then  you're going to turn your family away  and not going to have successful  relationships so I find it's important  that you have an office you know you're  going to the work and when you come home  you may be still you know you may get a  couple of ideas for your business write  them down or send them and send an email  to yourself don't let it take over your  day so that you know when you're  supposed to be saying time with your  family you're still thinking about work  and doing work if your home is your  office then it's a lot easier to blur  the lines and always be working compared  to if you have to have an office to go  to you know that that's your time for  work and then your hometown is your time  to be at home in my case right now I  schedule I'm in the office five hours a  day from Monday to Thursday and the rest  of the time I'm at home or dancing or  doing some of my son or whatever  whatever is on the schedule I find that  to do that effectively it's enough time  so if I have 20 hours a week that's  enough time to do everything you need to  do for my business but I need that time  to be able to actually do it so I need  those 20 hours would be highly focused  and really attentive on doing what I  need to do for my business can't afford  to be sidetracked thinking about other  things are getting distracted otherwise  instead of taking 20 hours it takes me  30 hours of 40 hours because I've been  so distracted and interrupted then it's  a lot harder to get your project done so  the pitch to your family might be I want  to spend more time with you guys but to  do that I need to be able to really  focus on my works that when I'm working  I'm working and then when I'm with you  I'm with you so you can probably end up  working fewer hours between way more  productive in those hours and get maybe  even more work than then usually do and  then  more time to go and stand with your  family so hopefully that helps again  that's you know my experience if you  guys like this video please give it a  thumbs up I love seeing those coming  that makes me want to do more videos for  you guys and if you have a question  about a home office life or you want to  share your experience is what you're  doing or a different question for your  business I'd love to hear it for leave a  comment under the video I always read  the comments and try to respond to each  one what I can so thank you and you'll  see you on the next episode  you
 

